From david.gutierrez at hp.com  Fri Nov 12 16:23:21 2004
From: david.gutierrez at hp.com (Gutierrez, David (HP LAC Escalations))
Date: Fri, 12 Nov 2004 10:23:21 -0600
Subject: (no subject)
Message-ID: <F7CC2BBAEC71284E8B48A13CC3109371057FA6A6@cceexc22.americas.cpqcorp.net>

Do you get a boot prompt >> or it goes directly to the Linux?
 
If you get a boot prompt, then type show dev and ensure that your boot
device is the selected on. Otherwise use the command show bootdev_def
and set bootdev_def to select the booting disk in which you installed
Linux. 
 
>> show device  (This will show all the devices)
     
>>set bootdev_def dka0,dka100
 
>> boot 
 
 
Good luck!
 
Kind Regards, 
 
David 
 

